@host = https://localhost:8081

# Public endpoint: send no cookie and no Authorization header.
#
# No seeded product has an image, so every request below returns 404 on a fresh database.
# To see a 200 you first have to upload one through the backoffice, which needs a
# Manager or Owner session:
#   1. POST /api/v1/auth/login  with a demo login from the README
#   2. POST /api/v1/products/17/image  as multipart/form-data
# Then come back here.

### Image of an active product
# Expect 200 with the stored bytes, the stored Content-Type,
# Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, and an ETag
GET {{host}}/api/v1/storefront/products/17/image

### Revalidate with the ETag returned above
# Replace the value with the ETag from the previous response, quotes included
# Expect 304 with no body
GET {{host}}/api/v1/storefront/products/17/image
If-None-Match: "REPLACE-WITH-THE-ETAG"

### Active product that has no image
# Expect 404 with a ProblemDetails body
GET {{host}}/api/v1/storefront/products/1/image

### Inactive product
# Expect 404 — the image route must not leak what the detail route hides
GET {{host}}/api/v1/storefront/products/2/image

### Product that does not exist
# Expect 404
GET {{host}}/api/v1/storefront/products/999/image
